# Lustra — backend

## Module layout (per feature)

```
modules/<name>/
  api/       controllers + DTO re-exports (Zod from @lustra/contracts)
  app/       one use-case per operation — `hold-slot.usecase.ts`, `confirm-booking.usecase.ts`
  domain/    pure FSM / policy — `booking-status.machine.ts` (no Prisma, no HTTP)
  infra/     repositories — `booking.repository.ts` (Prisma + raw SQL when needed)
```

## Hard rules

- Filenames: **kebab-case** (`hold-slot.usecase.ts`). Class names: PascalCase (`HoldSlotUseCase`).
- **No god services.** Prefer `*.usecase.ts` ≤ 300 lines; split by operation, not by dumping into `BookingsService`.
- Controllers: thin — parse → call use-case → map DTO. No business logic.
- Authz: `JwtGuard` + `RolesGuard` + ownership check inside use-case. `masterId`/`userId` from `@CurrentUser()`, never from body.
- Validation: **Zod pipe from contracts on every input**. Backend is the hard gate; reject unknown fields.
- Errors: `DomainError(code, httpStatus, message, details?)` → filter → `{ error: { code, message, details, requestId } }`.
- Transactions: short; no Telegram/HTTP/file I/O inside. Domain events via `OutboxEvent` in same TX.
- Private fields stripped in mappers — write tests that client DTOs lack `masterNote` / `trustScore`.
- Imports: `@/` aliases **everywhere** (e.g. `@/modules/master-profile/app/...`) — no `../` across folders.
- Env checks: use shared `isProduction` helper — never inline `process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production'`.
- Magic strings/codes (`P2002`, race markers): named constants / maps.

## Nest patterns to use

- Guards for auth/roles; interceptors for idempotency/logging; pipes for Zod.
- Throttler on `/auth/*` and sensitive mutations.
- Inject `Clock` for time; never `Date.now()` scattered in domain if testability matters.

## Anti-patterns

```ts
// ❌ fat service with 20 public methods
@Injectable() class BookingsService { create(){} cancel(){} … }

// ✅ one use-case per mutation
@Injectable() class HoldSlotUseCase { execute(input: HoldSlotInput) { … } }
```
